<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Republic of Ghana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ghana is a country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, independent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1957 and the first sub-Saharan colony to gain independence. It was the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a> and took its name from the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a>, which lay far to the north-west in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghana.jpg" alt="Ghana" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodosia Okoh · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ghana.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
